Enable the generic widescreen / ultrawide aspect path.

Applied to the vendored psxrecomp tree.

WHY: the framework already implements widescreen fully and generically (see
WIDESCREEN.md -- GTE X-squash via gte_set_display_aspect, per-prim proportion
correction so sprites/HUD are not stretched, HUD edge anchoring, FMV 4:3
pillarbox, authentic 4:3 BIOS boot), and `[video] aspect_ratio = "W:H"` is
parsed and validated in config_loader.cpp. The only thing preventing it is a
POLICY gate: upstream treats widescreen as "mod-owned" on PSX, to be activated
by trusted mod plugins rather than a generic setting. These two constexprs
drive a clamp (~main.cpp:11349) that forces any non-4:3 aspect back to 4:3.
There is no environment override, unlike frame interpolation.

This is a deliberate override of a DISTRIBUTION POLICY, not a technical limit,
and is appropriate for a personal build only. Do not propose it upstream.

STATUS: the clamp is gone -- the runtime now logs
    "widescreen 16:9 (native-wide, present 1:1; engages at game entry)"
instead of "clamping display aspect 16:9 -> 4:3". However the wider field of
view does NOT yet visibly engage in Crash 2; the rendered image stays 4:3.
Diagnosing that needs a -DPSX_DEBUG_TOOLS=ON build so the TCP debug server
(ws_aspect / ws_census / gpu_state's ws.{configured,active,game_mode}) is
compiled in -- the stock build sets PSX_NO_DEBUG_TOOLS=1 and strips it.

